      "text": "\\begin{align*}\nx^2 + y^2 &= (x - 5)^2 - 5^2 + (y + 3)^2 - 3^2 \\\\\n&= (x - 5)^2 + (y + 3)^2 - 25\n\\end{align*}\n\nSince $x^2 + y^2 = 10x - 6y - 34$, we can substitute to obtain:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n(x - 5)^2 + (y + 3)^2 - 25 &= (10x - 6y - 34) - 25 \\\\\n&= 10(x - 5) - 6(y + 3) \\\\\n&= 10x - 6y - 34\n\\end{align*}\n\nRemoving parentheses from each side gives us:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n(x - 5)^2 + (y + 3)^2 &= 10x - 6y - 34\n\\end{align*}\n\nThe expression on the left side is the square of a binomial, so we can equate the squared binomial to $(10x - 6y) - 34$:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n(x - 5)^2 + (y + 3)^2 &= \\sqrt{(10x - 6y - 34)^2} \\\\\n25^2 &= 34^2 \\implies 25^2 = 34^2 \\\\\n-5^2 + (-3)^2 &= 10x - 6y - 34 \\\\\n-25 = 10x - 6y - 34\n\\end{align*}\n\nSolving for $x$ and $y$:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n-25 + 25 &= 10x - 6y \\\\\n0 &= 10x - 6y - 34 \\\\\n10x - 6y &= 34 \\\\\nx + y &= 3\n\\end{align*}\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $\\boxed{3}$.",
